<Layout title="Home | Homological Alice">
	<h1>Homological Alice</h1>
	<p>
		I am an Honours student whose interests centre on mirror symmetry, symplectic geometry and
		symplectic topology, algebraic geometry—particularly geometric invariant theory (GIT) and
		tropical geometry—and geometric representation theory. I work under the supervision of Brett
		Parker and also receive extensive guidance from Yixuan Li.
	</p>
	<p>
		I expect to graduate at the end of 2026, by which time I will have completed my undergraduate
		thesis. Afterwards, I plan to devote myself to the study and research of exploded manifolds, with
		a particular interest in the connection between Gromov–Witten invariants and tropical geometry.
	</p>
	<p>
		I plan to announce my first preprint on arXiv in September or October 2026. It will be my first
		serious presentation of new mathematical results—please stay tuned.
	</p>
	<p>
		Alongside mathematics, I am developing an AVG game that I expect to release on Steam in 2027. I
		hope its writing will move you.
	</p>
</Layout>
